  "improvement": {
    "owning_skills": [
      "stream-processing-design"
    ],
    "mechanism": "Extend stream-processing-design state and history guidance with the concurrent snapshot and CDC recovery tuple: snapshot cursor, source log position, durable checkpoint, replication slot and required retained log. Reconcile snapshot rows against overlapping changes at a defined fence. Budget source log retention by write rate, maximum acknowledgement interval and lag, while diagnosing old open transactions separately.",
    "reading_and_contract_limits": "Both selected article bodies were read completely. Connector documentation and runtime examples were not executed or independently verified against a deployed version. XID-limited recovery misses deletes, physical row identifiers weaken guarantees, read-only low-traffic capture may need a published heartbeat, and Only Changes cannot supply prior history to a later destination.",
    "discriminating_case": "Interrupt a backfill at 80 percent, then delete a row and invalidate its replication slot during the outage. With the recovery tuple intact, resume from the durable checkpoint. With required WAL missing, require a new log position and reconciliation; reject restart-only or XID-only recovery as proof that deletes are correct."
  },
